issue.body:
A non-compliant Anthropic upstream sends `message_start` with `"usage":{}` (no `input_tokens` / `output_tokens`). Cursor Private Inference validates that event with zod and requires both counts to be numbers, so it aborts the turn and retries in silence. GPT is unaffected because it uses the Responses API. magpie relays `anthropic` to `anthropic` as-is, so the bad event reaches the client. A reply magpie itself translates already writes both counts.

This cannot be opened as a pull request: an owner of this repository has limited pull requests to collaborators. The change is one commit on top of `bf2e067e`, `be6309f44deb66df0b8b68eff120216891fb1f5a`, on `qiangxinglin/magpie` branch `gateway-fill-message-start-usage`.

## What changes

In `passthrough`, beside `intTidy`, `usageTidy` parses a relayed Messages reply and, only when `message_start.usage` is missing `input_tokens` or `output_tokens` (empty object, null, missing `usage`, or just one of the two), writes the missing count as `0`. `message_delta` still carries the real counts and is not rewritten. An event that already has both numbers goes byte for byte. A whole `type:message` reply is filled the same way.

Subsystem note: [docs/subsystems/gateway-routing.md](docs/subsystems/gateway-routing.md).

## Apply

```
curl -fsSL https://github.com/qiangxinglin/magpie/commit/be6309f44deb66df0b8b68eff120216891fb1f5a.patch | git am
```

Or save the patch below and `git am` that file. It applies onto `bf2e067e`.

## Tests

- `gofmt -l` on the changed Go files: clean
- `go vet -tags nogui ./internal/gateway/`
- `go test -tags nogui -count=1 -run "TestPassthroughFills|TestPassthroughLeaves|TestUsageTidy|TestPassthroughStreamWhole|TestPassthroughStreamCutMidLine|TestPassthroughRewritesModel" ./internal/gateway/`
- With the fill turned off, `TestPassthroughFillsEmptyMessageStartUsage` fails: `message_start.usage counts are not numbers: {}`
- Full `go test -tags nogui ./...` was not run
- A live Cursor Private Inference turn was not run

## Patch

```From be6309f44deb66df0b8b68eff120216891fb1f5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xinglin Qiang <xinglinqiang@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:23:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: fill missing Anthropic message_start usage so a
 strict client accepts a relayed stream

A relay that sends usage:{} on message_start makes Cursor Private Inference abort and retry. Passthrough writes the missing input_tokens and output_tokens as 0; a reply that already has both numbers stays byte for byte, and message_delta still carries the real counts.

Run: gofmt -l clean; go vet -tags nogui ./internal/gateway/; go test -tags nogui -count=1 -run "TestPassthroughFills|TestPassthroughLeaves|TestUsageTidy|TestPassthroughStreamWhole|TestPassthroughStreamCutMidLine|TestPassthroughRewritesModel" ./internal/gateway/. Without the fill, TestPassthroughFillsEmptyMessageStartUsage fails with "message_start.usage counts are not numbers: {}".
Not tried: the full suite, or a live Cursor Private Inference turn.
